.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-gpu-setup
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
None
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-gpu-setup
command detects available video hardware and guides the user
in selecting an appropriate direct rendering module (DRM) and
X11 driver.  It then deinstalls all DRMs and drivers, installs
the selected ones, and loads the selected DRM, and reconfigures
the system to load it at boot time.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

